Z||000002||1FST2M6||11-13-2000||01:42 PM||||WECOME TO THE FORUM!<P>yes 18s will fit 19" s will fit.. but ONLY pirelli makes a 235-35-19 and at $325 (US) each it's kinda steep! <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstlow.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstlow.jpg</A>  &lt;--my car with 17s. Hyptnoise has 18s on his car. 18x7.5 45mm offset 5x100 bolt pattern. you can call or e-mail NOPI at <A HREF="http://www.nopi.com" TARGET=_blank>www.nopi.com</A>  and get part #60210 suspension techniques 1.5" drop for $150.46 plus shipping and handeling.. find a local KYB dealer and get a set or go to <A HREF="http://www.shox.com" TARGET=_blank>www.shox.com</A>  and order a set of KYBs or KONIs. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/in-n-out.jpg</A>  &lt;my old car with a 10 in the floor and an Xtant 1001dx behind the seat. would hit 141db.  as for the PS.. uum i dunno.. <P><BR>--------------<BR>"Fondue forks for everybody"<BR> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 11-13-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||jonny_blaze||11-13-2000||04:12 PM||||awesome, thank you very much. with that lowering kit, will it contain everything nessesary, or do i need to buy other products as well?||||reg||1
Z||000004||william_thorniii||11-13-2000||04:17 PM||||jonny,<P>Also there is the option of going with coil-overs in the rear and dropped spindles in the front.  This is the path that I have chosen.  It is slightly more expensive but if you are going to be really pushing your car to its cornering limits... might be well worth it.  The vendors I chose were Ryane Motorsports (rear coil over kit.. not around anymore) and Street Dreams (drop spindles).  Of course I also bought new shocks/struts as well.  <P>Just another option,<P><BR>William T. Thorn, III||||reg||3
